# Gitleaks ignore list — reviewed, known false positives.
#
# Gitleaks scans the FULL git history (`gitleaks detect --all`), so a finding
# stays reported even after the offending line is fixed in the working tree —
# the old commit still contains it. Each fingerprint below has been manually
# reviewed and confirmed NOT to be a real secret. Format is:
#   <commit-sha>:<file>:<rule-id>:<start-line>
#
# Anything NOT listed here is still flagged with the full default ruleset, so
# a genuine leak elsewhere continues to fail the secrets-scan gate.

